{
    "format": "qucs-s multiphysics 1",
    "title": "A germanium-on-silicon waveguide photodiode",
    "description": "A lateral p-i-n of germanium grown on a silicon waveguide - its tensile strain narrowing the direct gap to 0.773 eV - 0.45 µm thick, its intrinsic part 0.7 µm wide between p⁺ and n⁺ germanium, 15 µm long (the model's thickness), reversed by 1 V. The waveguide's light, 1 mW at 1550 nm, is drawn up into the germanium (neff 3.84), whose direct gap absorbs it: 1.9 dB per µm, all but all of it over the length. Each photon absorbed across the gap makes a pair (Optical Generation, from emw.Qgap): 7.8e15 per second; the field collects 92 % of them - 1.14 mA, a responsivity of 1.14 A/W (the ideal qλ/hc 1.25 A/W). Dark, 7.2 nA. Modulated, the photocurrent falls to 1/√2 of its own at about 27 GHz - the carriers' transit, and those made in the doped germanium diffusing out slowly; its 6.6 fF through 50 Ω hardly adds. Along the wavelength - the mode followed from 1500 nm - 1.10 to 1.14 A/W to 1580 nm, then the strained edge: 0.89 A/W at 1600 nm, 0.42 at 1620, 0.16 at 1640 - the Franz-Keldysh effect's tail at the bias's field. Up through the germanium into the silicon, the heterojunction: the valence band 0.52 eV higher in the germanium (Anderson's rule), its holes kept there.",
    "parameters": [
        {
            "name": "Va",
            "expression": "-1[V]",
            "description": "the anode's voltage (reverse: negative)"
        },
        {
            "name": "P",
            "expression": "1[mW]",
            "description": "the light fed, in the silicon waveguide's mode"
        },
        {
            "name": "lambda",
            "expression": "1550[nm]",
            "description": "its wavelength"
        },
        {
            "name": "w",
            "expression": "0.7[um]",
            "description": "the intrinsic germanium's width"
        }
    ],
    "components": [
        {
            "unit": "um",
            "thickness": "15[um]",
            "geometry": [
                {
                    "type": "rectangle",
                    "label": "box",
